From 94e27769f7c11256f4da52c8aa79192f3f826be6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Virtroid build <build@virtroid.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 07:48:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gnss: report the location source's sky, NMEA and receiver

The default HAL reports made-up data wherever it has none of its own: a fixed list of 13 satellites, the NMEA line "$TEST,0,1,2,3,4,5", the hardware name "Google, Cuttlefish, AIDL v3", mock raw measurements and navigation messages, batched fixes at a fixed position, and a debug position in Mountain View. Each tells an app that looks that the device is an emulator.

Virtroid's node sends the sky and the NMEA sentences with each fix (deploy/aosp/gnss-feed.md). Report them, the sky with every fix, so a fix carries the satellites used in it whether or not an app listens, and ask the source at start which receiver the device has (CMD_GET_RECEIVER): its name and year, whether it measures carrier phase, and the signals it tracks. Advertise only capabilities this HAL backs, and report no measurements, navigation messages, batched fixes or debug position it does not have.

Change-Id: I67d1579758f7f3cdcc42c9a109002a6ed755965e
